  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Jimmy Buffett was an American singer-songwriter who blended country, folk and Caribbean influences into songs about escape and coastal life. His hit Margaritaville became the centre of a business spanning restaurants, resorts and consumer products. Decades of touring and recording built his fortune and a devoted audience whose members called themselves Parrot Heads.",
    "html": "<p>Jimmy Buffett was an American singer-songwriter who blended country, folk and Caribbean influences into songs about escape and coastal life. His hit Margaritaville became the centre of a business spanning restaurants, resorts and consumer products. Decades of touring and recording built his fortune and a devoted audience whose members called themselves Parrot Heads.</p>\r\n",
